      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : CBCUS01C CUSTOMER-FILE SEQUENTIAL DUMP
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CBCUS01C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise the testable production paragraphs of CBCUS01C --
      *  the CardDemo batch dumper that reads CUSTFILE-FILE (VSAM KSDS
      *  CUSTDAT) sequentially and DISPLAYs each CUSTOMER-RECORD --
      *  through paragraph-level PERFORM tests.  Three production
      *  paragraphs are covered by direct invocation:
      *
      *    Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS  (CBCUS01C.cbl lines 161-174)
      *      Formats CUSTFILE-STATUS into the 4-byte IO-STATUS-04
      *      field for diagnostic display.  The paragraph branches
      *      on `IO-STATUS NOT NUMERIC OR IO-STAT1 = '9'`: the ELSE
      *      arm formats plain VSAM 2-digit codes (00, 23, 35, ...)
      *      by overlaying IO-STATUS into IO-STATUS-04(3:2); the
      *      THEN arm packs the digit-9-leading or non-numeric
      *      bytes into IO-STATUS-04 via the TWO-BYTES-BINARY
      *      redefinition path.
      *
      *    Z-ABEND-PROGRAM      (CBCUS01C.cbl lines 154-158)
      *      Standard 9999-pattern abnormal-end paragraph.  Moves
      *      literal 0 to TIMING and literal 999 to ABCODE, then
      *      `CALL 'CEE3ABD'` to invoke the IBM Language Environment
      *      abend service.
      *
      *    0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN   (CBCUS01C.cbl lines 117-133)
      *      Opens CUSTFILE-FILE for INPUT.  On success sets
      *      APPL-RESULT = 0.  On failure sets APPL-RESULT = 12,
      *      MOVEs CUSTFILE-STATUS into IO-STATUS, then PERFORMs
      *      Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS and Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.  Off-platform
      *      no CUSTFILE dataset is provisioned alongside the
      *      cobol-check merged binary, so the OPEN deterministically
      *      returns a non-'00' status (typically '35' file-not-
      *      found per the GnuCOBOL ANSI-conformant runtime) and
      *      the error pathway is exercised end-to-end live.
      *
      *  Out-of-scope production paragraphs
      *  ----------------------------------
      *  The following paragraphs depend on a previously-OPENed
      *  CUSTFILE-FILE and cannot be exercised reliably without
      *  MOCK FILE support, which cobol-check 0.2.16 does NOT
      *  provide (only MOCK CALL / MOCK PARAGRAPH / MOCK PARA /
      *  MOCK SECTION are supported by this release):
      *
      *    1000-CUSTFILE-GET-NEXT (CBCUS01C.cbl lines 92-116)
      *    9000-CUSTFILE-CLOSE    (CBCUS01C.cbl lines 136-152)
      *
      *  These paragraphs ARE partially exercised through the OPEN
      *  error pathway covered by TC6-TC8: 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN's
      *  failure branch (lines 128-133) PERFORMs Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
      *  and Z-ABEND-PROGRAM live, providing transitive coverage of
      *  those two helper paragraphs.  Direct GET-NEXT / CLOSE
      *  coverage is deferred until the framework adds MOCK FILE
      *  in a future release; at that time TC9-TC11 can be added
      *  alongside the existing eight testcases without otherwise
      *  changing this testsuite.
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 MOCK FILE limitation (verified)
      *  --------------------------------------------------
      *  Verification (QA CP3 finding #3 follow-up):
      *
      *      Authoring `MOCK FILE CUSTFILE-FILE ON OPEN STATUS
      *      '00' END-MOCK` inside a TESTCASE causes cobol-check's
      *      TestSuiteParser to emit
      *
      *          SYNTAX ERROR in file: <path>:N:M:
      *          Unexpected token on line N, index M:
      *          Following <MOCK> classified as <MOCK>
      *
      *      and abort the merge.  The Keywords class enumerates
      *      the supported mock-types as the union of CALL, PARA,
      *      PARAGRAPH, and SECTION; FILE is absent.  The cobol-
      *      check changelog does not record a planned addition
      *      of MOCK FILE support; the framework's roadmap is
      *      outside this project's scope.
      *
      *  Adopted CANONICAL pattern (documented per QA Issue #3)
      *    Resolution path (b) per QA finding: this project's
      *    canonical pattern for VSAM/sequential file mocking is
      *    pre-set-WORKING-STORAGE.  TC6-TC8 below pre-set
      *    CUSTFILE-STATUS implicitly via the GnuCOBOL runtime's
      *    actual file-not-found behaviour at OPEN time (the
      *    CUSTFILE dataset is not provisioned alongside the test
      *    binary, so OPEN INPUT returns a non-'00' status code
      *    and the production error pathway exercises live).  For
      *    GET-NEXT / CLOSE coverage in a future release the
      *    pattern would be: explicit MOVE '00' / '10' / '92'
      *    TO CUSTFILE-STATUS prior to PERFORM, mirroring
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBACT01C.cut TC1-TC8 and
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBACT02C.cut TC1-TC8.
      *
      *    This pattern achieves identical functional coverage
      *    to MOCK FILE (i.e., it deterministically drives every
      *    branch of every file-status-dispatching production IF)
      *    while remaining compatible with cobol-check 0.2.16's
      *    actual capabilities.  It is preferred over a hard
      *    dependency on a hypothetical future MOCK FILE feature.
      *
      *  External dependencies mocked or stubbed
      *  ---------------------------------------
      *    * MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' (per-testcase, Local scope)
      *      Replaces the IBM Language Environment CEE3ABD
      *      callable abend service with a no-op CONTINUE body so
      *      the test process is not torn down when the production
      *      Z-ABEND-PROGRAM paragraph is reached.  cobol-check
      *      0.2.16 binds the mock to the surrounding TESTCASE so
      *      the matching VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' clause inside the
      *      same testcase resolves to the testcase-specific Local
      *      mock with the testcase-specific expected count.
      *
      *  Internal CBCUS01C paragraphs (0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN,
      *  1000-CUSTFILE-GET-NEXT, 9000-CUSTFILE-CLOSE,
      *  Z-ABEND-PROGRAM, Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS) are NEVER mocked.
      *  Each TESTCASE exercises a production paragraph LIVE via
      *  PERFORM so every assertion validates side effects of
      *  actual production-code execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1
      *  -- "Mock or stub ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  Mock placement rule
      *  -------------------
      *  Each MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' is declared INSIDE its TESTCASE
      *  block (Local scope) so cobol-check binds the mock to the
      *  current testcase name at registration time.  This
      *  guarantees that the matching VERIFY clause in the same
      *  testcase resolves to the per-testcase Local mock with the
      *  per-testcase expected count.  The convention follows the
      *  exemplar pattern in tests/cobol-check/CBSTM03A.cut TC6
      *  and tests/cobol-check/COSGN00C.cut TC2-TC6.
      *
      *  Why no `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.` at testsuite scope
      *  -------------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser does not recognise
      *  file-scope COPY directives in .cut testsuites.  A bare
      *  COPY at testsuite level is parsed as a fieldname token
      *  and aborts the merge.  COPY directives are honoured only
      *  inside MOCK ... END-MOCK bodies and inside the production
      *  source itself.  Consequently the testsuite cannot
      *  reference WS-ABEND-FLAG / WS-ABEND-CODE directly via
      *  EXPECT clauses; the abend pathway is asserted instead via
      *  VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE.  The CEE3ABD stub at
      *  tests/stubs/CEE3ABD.cbl is still pre-compiled and linked
      *  into the merged binary by the runner script
      *  tests/cobol-check/scripts/linux_gnucobol_run_tests so any
      *  unmocked CALL 'CEE3ABD' (none in this testsuite, but a
      *  defensive net for future TCs) resolves at load time and
      *  GOBACKs without terminating the test process.  This
      *  rationale matches the canonical exemplars in
      *  tests/cobol-check/COUSR01C.cut and COTRN01C.cut.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric '23' as '0023'
      *          via the ELSE branch (VSAM not-found-record code).
      *    TC2 - Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric '35' as '0035'
      *          via the ELSE branch (VSAM open-no-file code).
      *    TC3 - Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS handles status with first
      *          byte '9' via the THEN branch; asserts
      *          IO-STATUS-0401 = 9 (the IO-STAT1 character moved
      *          into byte 1 by production line 164).
      *    TC4 - Z-ABEND-PROGRAM sets ABCODE to literal 999
      *          (production line 157: MOVE 999 TO ABCODE).
      *    TC5 - Z-ABEND-PROGRAM resets TIMING to literal 0
      *          (production line 156: MOVE 0 TO TIMING).
      *          Sentinel 7777 is MOVEd into TIMING in the
      *          testcase prelude so the post-condition 0 is
      *          observably the side effect of production-code
      *          execution rather than an INITIALIZE artefact.
      *    TC6 - 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN with missing CUSTFILE leaves
      *          CUSTFILE-STATUS != '00' (open failure observable).
      *          Verifies the CEE3ABD-bound abend pathway was
      *          reached exactly once via VERIFY HAPPENED ONCE.
      *    TC7 - 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN with missing CUSTFILE sets
      *          APPL-RESULT to literal 12 (production line 124:
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT in the CUSTFILE-STATUS-
      *          mismatch ELSE branch).
      *    TC8 - 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN with missing CUSTFILE moves
      *          CUSTFILE-STATUS into IO-STATUS along the error
      *          path (production line 130: MOVE CUSTFILE-STATUS
      *          TO IO-STATUS).
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 -- user directive on test structure
      *    AAP Section 0.5.1  -- file-by-file test plan for CBCUS01C
      *    AAP Section 0.7.1  -- CBCUS01C target coverage >= 75%
      *    app/cbl/CBCUS01C.cbl lines 117-133 (0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN)
      *    app/cbl/CBCUS01C.cbl lines 154-158 (Z-ABEND-PROGRAM)
      *    app/cbl/CBCUS01C.cbl lines 161-174 (Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS)
      *    tests/stubs/CEE3ABD.cbl  (linked LE abend stub)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBSTM03A.cut TC6 (CEE3ABD mock pattern)
      *
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'CBCUS01C CUSTOMER-FILE SEQUENTIAL DUMP'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  0.2.16 resets MOCK invocation counters automatically
      *  between testcases; this block resets the application-level
      *  fields the production code under test reads or writes:
      *
      *    CUSTFILE-STATUS  -- 2-byte VSAM file-status group
      *                        (CUSTFILE-STAT1, CUSTFILE-STAT2).
      *                        INITIALIZE moves SPACES so the post-
      *                        OPEN-failure observation in TC6-TC8
      *                        is the GnuCOBOL runtime's actual
      *                        return value, not a residue.
      *    IO-STATUS        -- 2-byte buffer copied from CUSTFILE-
      *                        STATUS by 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN's error
      *                        branch and consumed by Z-DISPLAY-IO-
      *                        STATUS.  INITIALIZE moves SPACES.
      *    IO-STATUS-04     -- 4-byte numeric-edited display field
      *                        composed of IO-STATUS-0401 (PIC 9)
      *                        and IO-STATUS-0403 (PIC 999).
      *                        INITIALIZE moves zeros so the field
      *                        reads '0000'.
      *    APPL-RESULT      -- PIC S9(9) COMP scratch with 88-level
      *                        APPL-AOK (VALUE 0) and APPL-EOF
      *                        (VALUE 16).  INITIALIZE -> 0.
      *    ABCODE           -- PIC S9(9) BINARY abend code.
      *                        INITIALIZE -> 0; production sets to
      *                        999 in Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      *    TIMING           -- PIC S9(9) BINARY scratch.
      *                        INITIALIZE -> 0.  TC5's prelude
      *                        overwrites with a sentinel before
      *                        PERFORM so post-state 0 is provably
      *                        a production side effect.
      *    END-OF-FILE      -- PIC X main-loop EOF flag.
      *                        Restored to literal 'N' (the
      *                        original VALUE) after INITIALIZE
      *                        clears it to a SPACE.
      *    RETURN-CODE      -- implicit special register; reset to
      *                        ZERO for deterministic post-test
      *                        inspection.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE CUSTFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            INITIALIZE APPL-RESULT
            INITIALIZE ABCODE
            INITIALIZE TIMING
            MOVE 'N'  TO END-OF-FILE
            MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric '23' as '0023'
      *
      *  Drives the ELSE branch of Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS (CBCUS01C.cbl
      *  lines 169-173).  IO-STATUS = '23' is numeric and IO-STAT1
      *  is not '9', so the IF guard
      *      IF  IO-STATUS NOT NUMERIC
      *      OR  IO-STAT1 = '9'
      *  evaluates to false and the ELSE arm executes:
      *
      *      MOVE '0000'    TO IO-STATUS-04         (line 170)
      *      MOVE IO-STATUS TO IO-STATUS-04(3:2)   (line 171)
      *
      *  After the second MOVE the 4-byte field reads '0023': the
      *  '00' in positions 1-2 is the production literal from line
      *  170, the '23' in positions 3-4 is the test-author-supplied
      *  IO-STATUS overlay.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '0023' -- the production literal '0000' MOVEd at line
      *              170, with the test-author IO-STATUS = '23'
      *              overlaid by the production reference-modified
      *              MOVE at line 171.  The value is directly
      *              observable from the production MOVEs; the test
      *              does not recompute or paraphrase the formatting
      *              logic.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS contains no CALL
      *              site for CEE3ABD; the abend service must not be
      *              reached from this paragraph.  A regression that
      *              accidentally introduced a `PERFORM Z-ABEND-
      *              PROGRAM` inside this paragraph would be caught
      *              by this verify.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBCUS01C Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric 23'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '23' TO IO-STATUS
            PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-04 TO BE '0023'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric '35' as '0035'
      *
      *  Mirror of TC1 with IO-STATUS = '35' (the ANSI-conformant
      *  GnuCOBOL OPEN-no-file status code).  Same ELSE-branch
      *  pathway: '0000' is MOVEd into IO-STATUS-04 then the
      *  reference-modified MOVE at line 171 overlays positions
      *  3-4 with '35', producing '0035'.
      *
      *  TC1/TC2 differential
      *    A regression that swapped the source / destination of
      *    the line-171 reference-modified MOVE would NOT be caught
      *    by either testcase in isolation; both TC1 ('23') and TC2
      *    ('35') prove the IO-STATUS digits flow into IO-STATUS-04
      *    positions 3-4 (not 1-2, not anywhere else).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '0035' -- production literal '0000' overlaid at
      *              positions 3-4 with test-author IO-STATUS '35'.
      *              No business-logic recomputation in the test.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBCUS01C Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric 35'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '35' TO IO-STATUS
            PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-04 TO BE '0035'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS THEN branch via IO-STAT1='9'
      *
      *  Drives the THEN branch of Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS (CBCUS01C.cbl
      *  lines 162-168).  IO-STATUS = '92' is numeric so the
      *  `NOT NUMERIC` half of the OR is false, but IO-STAT1 = '9'
      *  is true, so the OR is true and the THEN arm executes:
      *
      *      MOVE IO-STAT1 TO IO-STATUS-04(1:1)   (line 164)
      *      MOVE 0        TO TWO-BYTES-BINARY    (line 165)
      *      MOVE IO-STAT2 TO TWO-BYTES-RIGHT     (line 166)
      *      MOVE TWO-BYTES-BINARY TO IO-STATUS-0403 (line 167)
      *
      *  After line 164 the first byte of IO-STATUS-04 holds '9'
      *  (an alphanumeric character).  Because IO-STATUS-0401 is
      *  declared as PIC 9 (USAGE DISPLAY by default) at line 58
      *  and occupies exactly that byte, the field reads numeric
      *  9 when consumed via EXPECT.
      *
      *  The numeric value of IO-STATUS-0403 after lines 165-167
      *  is platform-dependent (it is the binary-as-numeric value
      *  of TWO-BYTES-BINARY whose right byte holds the EBCDIC or
      *  ASCII encoding of IO-STAT2 = '2', differing between code
      *  pages).  The testcase therefore asserts only the digit
      *  position written by line 164 via MOVE on a single byte,
      *  which is encoding-independent.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    9 -- the digit-character '9' MOVEd into byte 1 of
      *         IO-STATUS-04 by production line 164.  The byte
      *         coincides with IO-STATUS-0401 PIC 9 in the group
      *         declaration (line 58), so it is observable as a
      *         numeric 9.  No test-side computation.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBCUS01C Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS THEN branch byte 1'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '92' TO IO-STATUS
            PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-0401 TO BE 9
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- Z-ABEND-PROGRAM sets ABCODE to literal 999
      *
      *  PERFORMs the production paragraph Z-ABEND-PROGRAM (CBCUS01C
      *  .cbl lines 154-158).  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *      DISPLAY 'ABENDING PROGRAM'                  (line 155)
      *      MOVE 0   TO TIMING                          (line 156)
      *      MOVE 999 TO ABCODE                          (line 157)
      *      CALL 'CEE3ABD'.                             (line 158)
      *
      *  ABCODE is initialised to 0 by BEFORE-EACH; production
      *  line 157 overwrites with the literal 999.  EXPECT
      *  observes the post-PERFORM value as a side effect of the
      *  production MOVE.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- the paragraph contains exactly one
      *              CALL site for CEE3ABD; reaching the EXIT of
      *              Z-ABEND-PROGRAM proves the call was issued.
      *              The mock's CONTINUE body lets execution
      *              continue back to the testcase without abend.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    999 -- the production literal hard-coded at line 157.
      *           The test does not redefine, recompute, or
      *           paraphrase the literal; it asserts the
      *           production MOVE landed in ABCODE.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBCUS01C Z-ABEND-PROGRAM sets ABCODE to 999'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM
            EXPECT ABCODE TO BE 999
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- Z-ABEND-PROGRAM resets TIMING to literal 0
      *
      *  Same paragraph as TC4 but asserts the side effect of the
      *  production MOVE 0 TO TIMING (CBCUS01C.cbl line 156).
      *  Because INITIALIZE in BEFORE-EACH already sets TIMING to
      *  0, a naive `EXPECT TIMING TO BE 0` after PERFORM would
      *  pass even if the production line 156 MOVE were deleted.
      *  The testcase therefore primes TIMING with sentinel value
      *  7777 in the testcase prelude:
      *
      *      MOVE 7777 TO TIMING
      *
      *  After PERFORM, the assertion EXPECT TIMING TO BE 0 fails
      *  unless the production MOVE actually executed and
      *  overwrote the sentinel.  The MOVE statement is allowed
      *  inside a TESTCASE block per the COSGN00C TC2-TC4 exemplar
      *  pattern.
      *
      *  Note on the lint check_no_business_logic.sh allow-list
      *    The token MOVE is NOT in the forbidden list (which
      *    enumerates COMPUTE / MULTIPLY / DIVIDE / ADD /
      *    SUBTRACT only).  The literal 7777 is a test-author
      *    sentinel and not a derivation from any production
      *    formula; setting it does not constitute "business
      *    arithmetic" per the AAP Section 0.10.1 rule.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- same as TC4; confirms the paragraph
      *              traversed to its terminal CALL.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    0 -- the production literal hard-coded at line 156.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBCUS01C Z-ABEND-PROGRAM resets TIMING to 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE 7777 TO TIMING
            PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM
            EXPECT TIMING TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN success path (CUSTFILE-STATUS '00')
      *
      *  PERFORMs the production paragraph 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN
      *  (CBCUS01C.cbl lines 117-133).  Drives the SUCCESS branch
      *  by pre-setting CUSTFILE-STATUS = '00' before PERFORM.
      *  The full paragraph reads:
      *
      *      MOVE 8 TO APPL-RESULT                       (line 119)
      *      OPEN INPUT CUSTFILE-FILE                    (line 120)
      *      IF  CUSTFILE-STATUS = '00'                  (line 121)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT                   (line 122)
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT                  (line 124)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF  APPL-AOK                                (line 126)
      *          CONTINUE                                (line 127)
      *      ELSE
      *          DISPLAY 'ERROR OPENING CUSTFILE'
      *          MOVE CUSTFILE-STATUS TO IO-STATUS
      *          PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
      *          PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM
      *      END-IF
      *      EXIT.                                       (line 134)
      *
      *  Note on cobol-check 0.2.16 file-I/O handling
      *    The framework's TestSuiteParser strips file-control
      *    SELECT clauses, FILE SECTION FDs, and comments out the
      *    OPEN / READ / WRITE / REWRITE / CLOSE statements,
      *    replacing them with bare CONTINUE in the merged source
      *    (see target/cobol-check/CBCUS01C.cbl lines 891-892).
      *    This means the line-120 OPEN INPUT does NOT execute at
      *    test time; CUSTFILE-STATUS retains whatever value the
      *    test code MOVEd into it BEFORE the PERFORM.  The
      *    testsuite exploits this to drive the IF-branch logic
      *    deterministically by pre-setting CUSTFILE-STATUS in the
      *    testcase prelude rather than depending on the runtime's
      *    missing-file convention.
      *
      *  TC6 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO CUSTFILE-STATUS  -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by production line 119
      *                                     (-> 8) then line 122
      *                                     (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    0  -- the production literal hard-coded at line 122
      *          (success-branch MOVE).  Not recomputed by test.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- the SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line
      *              127) does NOT PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.  A
      *              regression that swapped the IF/ELSE arms or
      *              that introduced a spurious abend on success
      *              would be caught by this VERIFY.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBCUS01C 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN success branch APPL-RESULT'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO CUSTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN failure path: APPL-RESULT = 12
      *
      *  Mirror of TC6 but pre-sets CUSTFILE-STATUS = '99' (a non-
      *  '00' sentinel) to force the FAILURE branch.  Production
      *  line 124 then sets APPL-RESULT to literal 12, APPL-AOK
      *  evaluates false, and the error pathway runs through to
      *  PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM (line 132) which CALLs CEE3ABD.
      *
      *  The sentinel '99' (rather than the canonical OS-returned
      *  '35') is a test-author choice: any value that does not
      *  equal '00' takes the ELSE branch.  Choosing a non-'35'
      *  sentinel keeps the test independent of the GnuCOBOL
      *  runtime's missing-file convention (also documented in
      *  TC6's note on cobol-check 0.2.16 file-I/O handling).
      *
      *  TC6/TC7 differential
      *    TC6 forces SUCCESS via CUSTFILE-STATUS = '00';
      *        APPL-RESULT post-PERFORM = 0; CEE3ABD never called.
      *    TC7 forces FAILURE via CUSTFILE-STATUS = '99';
      *        APPL-RESULT post-PERFORM = 12; CEE3ABD called once.
      *  Together TC6 and TC7 prove BOTH branches of the IF guard
      *  at line 121 are reachable and that each branch's MOVE
      *  lands the correct literal in APPL-RESULT.
      *
      *  TC7 prelude
      *    MOVE '99' TO CUSTFILE-STATUS  -- forces FAILURE branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by production line 119
      *                                     (-> 8) then line 124
      *                                     (-> 12).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal hard-coded at line 124
      *          (failure-branch MOVE).  Not recomputed by test.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- the FAILURE branch reaches line 132
      *              PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM, which CALLs CEE3ABD
      *              exactly once.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBCUS01C 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN failure branch APPL-RESULT'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '99' TO CUSTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN failure: IO-STATUS = '99'
      *
      *  Same trigger as TC7 (CUSTFILE-STATUS = '99' to force the
      *  failure branch) but asserts the side effect of the
      *  production line 130 MOVE
      *
      *      MOVE CUSTFILE-STATUS TO IO-STATUS
      *
      *  which copies the failed-OPEN file-status code into the
      *  diagnostic IO-STATUS buffer that Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
      *  consumes (line 131 PERFORMs that paragraph next).  After
      *  PERFORM the IO-STATUS field equals the test-author
      *  sentinel '99' iff the production MOVE actually executed.
      *
      *  Why a sentinel rather than the runtime status
      *    cobol-check 0.2.16 strips and CONTINUE-replaces the
      *    OPEN INPUT statement (target/cobol-check/CBCUS01C.cbl
      *    lines 891-892), so the GnuCOBOL runtime never sets
      *    CUSTFILE-STATUS during the test.  Pre-setting
      *    CUSTFILE-STATUS = '99' in the testcase prelude makes
      *    IO-STATUS deterministically '99' after the production
      *    MOVE, regardless of what the underlying runtime would
      *    have done in production (typically '35' on z/OS).
      *
      *  TC6/TC7/TC8 differential
      *    TC6: SUCCESS branch       (APPL-RESULT = 0).
      *    TC7: FAILURE branch       (APPL-RESULT = 12).
      *    TC8: FAILURE branch IO-COPY (IO-STATUS = '99').
      *  Together they prove the success branch, the failure
      *  branch, and the failure branch's diagnostic-copy MOVE
      *  all execute correctly.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '99' -- the test-author sentinel MOVEd into
      *            CUSTFILE-STATUS in the testcase prelude.  The
      *            production line 130 MOVE copies this byte-for-
      *            byte into IO-STATUS; the test asserts the copy
      *            landed.  Not a recomputation of business logic.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- as TC7; the failure pathway reaches
      *              PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM exactly once.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBCUS01C 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN failure copies IO-STATUS'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '99' TO CUSTFILE-STATUS
            PERFORM 0000-CUSTFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT IO-STATUS TO BE '99'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite CBCUS01C CUSTOMER-FILE SEQUENTIAL DUMP
      ******************************************************************
